        "description": "CRATE_BOX WITH A STICKY LID, PARTIALLY OBSERVABLE\n\nOne agent, R, must open the crate_box.\n\nSkills (one skill per decision cycle):\n  OpenLid(agent, crate_box): lift the closed lid. A stuck lid never opens. A free lid always comes up.\n    The status is ok if the lid is open afterwards.\n  Tap(agent, crate_box): tap the closed lid. Tapping sometimes frees a stuck lid and never sticks a free\n    one. Status ok whenever the tap was made.\n    The agent then hears a sound (thud | click) that usually, but not always, tells whether the\n    lid is still stuck afterwards.\n\nHidden: whether the lid starts stuck is decided at random and never shown directly.\n\nObserved after every skill: whether the lid is open, the skill's status (ok | fail), and after Tap the sound.\n\nRewards: -0.05 per cycle, an extra -0.02 per tap, +5 when the crate_box is open. Discount 0.98.\n\nThe probabilities are NOT given: model each one as a named parameter.",
