        "description": "CRATE THAT MAY BE HEAVY, PARTIALLY OBSERVABLE\n\nTwo agents, A and B, must raise the crate together. It has two grip spots, front and back.\n\nSkills (one skill per decision cycle):\n  Approach(agent, spot), spot in {front, back}: step to a grip spot. A spot holds one agent,\n    and an agent never approaches the spot it already holds. Status ok.\n  JointLift(agent, crate, partner): the agent on front and the partner on back lift together.\n    A heavy crate never comes up. Even a light crate sometimes slips back down. The status is ok if the\n    crate is raised afterwards.\n  Probe(agent, crate): the agent on front tests the weight. The feel (strains | easy) is\n    usually, but not always, right about whether the crate is heavy. Status ok.\n\nHidden: whether the crate is heavy is decided at random at the start, never changes, and is never\nshown directly.\n\nObserved after every skill: which spot each agent holds, whether the crate is raised, the skill's\nstatus (ok | fail), and after Probe the feel.\n\nRewards: -0.01 per agent per cycle, an extra -0.1 per probe, +1 per agent when the crate is raised. Discount 0.9.\n\nThe probabilities are NOT given: model each one as a named parameter.",
